+# Aegis AI/ML Platform — Product View
+
+This document captures what "AI/ML platform" means for Aegis and the product scope we will deliver.
+
+Core product promise
+- Self‑service developer experience for ML teams to train, evaluate, promote, serve, and monitor models while preserving reproducibility, governance, observability, cost & carbon awareness, and operational safety.
+
+User-facing capabilities
+- Reproducible model builds and provenance: artifacts, manifests, dependency snapshots saved with model versions.
+- Automated training & promotion pipelines: triggers, CI gates, verifiers and promotion policies.
+- Serving: low‑latency Triton endpoints plus scalable batch serving.
+- Monitoring & drift detection: Prometheus SLIs, verifiers, shadow & canary tooling.
+- Governance: IdP & RBAC, wrapper audit, evidence capture & SME signoff flows.
+- Cost & carbon accounting and chargeback per team/model.
+- Extensibility & multi‑tenant support: plugins, custom tasks, quotas and isolation.
+
+Minimal architecture (control & data plane)
+- Control plane:
+  - Model Registry service (versions, metadata, lineage)
+  - Pipeline orchestration + interceptors (Tekton / Argo)
+  - Promotion controller + gates (accounting & verifiers)
+  - AuthN/AuthZ (Keycloak) + RBAC manager
+  - Evidence service (S3 with retention + signed manifests)
+- Data plane:
+  - Training clusters (GPU node pools, DCGM)
+  - Serving clusters (Triton + autoscaling)
+  - Ingest & preproc pipelines (resumable)
+- Observability & policies:
+  - Prometheus, Grafana, Alertmanager, OpenTelemetry
+  - Cost & carbon accounting + router + policy controller
+
+Developer UX
+- REST/GraphQL control-plane APIs, Python SDK, CLI, and Web UI (catalog, model cards, promotion flow).
+
+Roadmap pointers
+- Productize the Model Registry and Promotion Gate (first milestone)
+- Harden wrappers, run long dry‑runs, and complete long‑shadow evidence (safety milestone)
+- Enable carbon accounting + policy controller and enforce test budgets (sustainability milestone)
+
+Use this document as the canonical product view for engineering, SRE, security, and product stakeholders.
+
